version = 1
id = "daily-ai-digest-archive"
kind = "cron"
name = "Daily AI Digest Archive"
prompt = """
Before doing any research, determine the current time in Asia/Shanghai.

- If the current Asia/Shanghai time is not between 09:00:00 and 09:14:59, exit immediately with a concise no-op note and make no file or git changes.
- If it is within that window, compute today's digest path `daily/YYYY/YYYY-MM/YYYY-MM-DD.md` using the current Asia/Shanghai date. If the file already exists, exit immediately with a concise no-op note and make no file or git changes.
- If the file is missing, research and write the daily AI digest for the current scheduled run using the current workspace git repository as the archive.

Determine the report date in Asia/Shanghai and cover the window from the previous 09:00:00 to the current 09:00:00 Asia/Shanghai bucket using the automation schedule time; if schedule metadata is unavailable, fall back to the previous 24 hours and state that fallback explicitly in the report. Create or update `daily/YYYY/YYYY-MM/YYYY-MM-DD.md` with title `# AI 日报 - YYYY-MM-DD`. Follow the repository guidance in `README.md`, `docs/coverage-map.md`, `docs/editorial-guidelines.md`, `docs/source-watchlist.md`, and `docs/automation-spec.md`.

Time-window and novelty requirements:
- Primary reporting window is the prior 09:00 to current 09:00 Asia/Shanghai bucket.
- If that strict window has too few high-value confirmed updates, you may supplement with still-developing high-value official updates from the previous several days, but you must explicitly state the supplemental date range in the report.
- Supplemental items must avoid repeating items already covered in the repository's recent daily digests unless there is a materially new angle, update, or follow-up.
- If there is no sufficiently high-confidence new information, prefer a shorter digest rather than filler.

Data-source requirements:
- First scan the AI coding agent watchlist in `docs/source-watchlist.md`, including Codex, Claude Code, Cursor, GitHub Copilot, Gemini CLI, Devin, Qwen Code, and Z Code related product pages, blogs, docs, changelogs, releases, and official repositories.
- Then scan the China model company watchlist in `docs/source-watchlist.md`, including DeepSeek, Qwen, Zhipu, Kimi, MiniMax, Tencent Hunyuan, Baidu Wenxin, and ByteDance Doubao / Volcano Engine Ark related official product pages, docs, product updates, blogs, and GitHub orgs where available.
- If there are high-value adjacent signals that materially affect the AI competitive landscape, also scan the AI peripheral watchlist in `docs/source-watchlist.md`, including compute and semiconductors, cloud and datacenter capacity, policy and regulation, security and misuse governance, enterprise adoption, and high-value industry deployment.
- Scan the AI blogger watchlist in `docs/source-watchlist.md`, prioritizing the core daily radar of active AI bloggers and practitioners. Core radar sources may contribute high-value AI clues, tool discoveries, community signals, product updates, viewpoints, methodology notes, or practice reviews. Use low-frequency key-person candidates only when there is a public long-form post, public talk, major short post, route disagreement, strategic judgment, or key signal.
- Scan the AI research frontier watchlist in `docs/source-watchlist.md` for high-value papers, research blogs, benchmarks, evals, open-source implementations, and lab signals. For each included research item, prioritize the original paper or research source link. If there is a useful interpretation from an author, researcher, core maintainer, or credible technical blogger, include it as auxiliary interpretation, not as a replacement for the original source.
- For important tools and products, do not rely on a single homepage. Check the product page plus official docs plus changelog or release notes plus official GitHub or release activity when available.
- Prefer official primary sources first: company blogs, research pages, product docs, official GitHub repos, changelogs, release notes, product update pages, and official announcements. Use media coverage only as supporting context.
- Use dynamic update streams where relevant: changelog pages, release notes pages, GitHub releases, recent org activity, and documentation update pages.
- Prefer deep links to the exact changelog entry, release page, doc page, or article when possible instead of only top-level index pages.
- Treat personal viewpoints and curated social posts as clue or opinion samples, not as factual confirmation. Do not use a person's blog post, X/Twitter post, public comment, or curated roundup as the sole factual source for a news item; when practical, add the official source or original project link.

Content requirements:
- Focus on global AI hotspots with priority on Chinese and US model companies.
- Prioritize OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Meta, Microsoft, GitHub, DeepSeek, Qwen, Zhipu, Kimi, MiniMax, Baidu, Tencent, ByteDance, and notable open-source AI infrastructure.
- Pay special attention to AI coding agents and developer tools, including Codex, Claude Code, GitHub Copilot, Cursor, Devin, Gemini CLI, and important official company blogs or research posts behind those products.
- Expand beyond AI-only headlines when warranted, but keep the center of gravity on AI. Only include adjacent signals when they clearly feed back into AI competition, model deployment, developer workflows, governance, or adoption.
- Include clickable source links for every major item and use absolute dates instead of relative wording.
- Keep the digest concise and high signal.
- Include a short human-readable `结构化快照` near the top of the report following the repository template.
- Place the full machine-friendly YAML metadata in a `结构化索引` section later in the report, preferably inside a collapsible block, capturing at least date/window, supplemental range, themes, regions, companies, products, signals, opinion_sources, viewpoint_themes, research_sources, research_themes, research_artifacts, research_interpretations, followups, fact_confidence, and signal_strength.
- If high-value clues or opinion samples are included, add an `AI 圈博主` section with `类型：信息线索 / 观点判断 / 方法论 / 实践复盘`, `摘要`, `为什么值得记录`, `我的判断`, and `来源`. If there are no high-value clues or opinion samples, omit the body section and set `opinion_sources: []` and `viewpoint_themes: []` in YAML.
- If high-value research frontier items are included, add an `AI 研究前沿` section with `类型：论文 / 研究博客 / benchmark / eval / 开源实现 / 实验室动向`, `研究问题`, `核心思路`, `为什么可能影响未来`, `局限 / 待验证点`, `原文链接`, `权威解读`, and `我的判断`. If there are no high-value research frontier items, omit the body section and set `research_sources: []`, `research_themes: []`, `research_artifacts: []`, and `research_interpretations: []` in YAML.
- When adjacent signals are included, record them under `peripheral_themes` in the YAML metadata and summarize them in an `AI 外围情报观察` section. If there are no high-confidence adjacent signals, omit the body section and set `peripheral_themes: []`.
- Use `fact_confidence` for source reliability and `signal_strength` for how important the day's signal is; do not use one generic confidence value for both.
- Reuse stable labels for themes, companies, and products where possible so later weekly/monthly summaries can aggregate them consistently.
- Include a dedicated `今日评论与判断` section. This section must synthesize the three radars (`AI 新闻`, `AI 圈博主`, and `AI 研究前沿`) and go beyond summarizing facts to capture the day's independent judgment about competitive dynamics, product momentum, technical direction, workflow change, weak signals versus real trends, and what is worth tracking next.
- Make it explicit that the judgment section is based on the current report's sample of confirmed facts.
- For changing metrics such as stars, trending position, release cadence, or similar snapshots, include a date, version number, or snapshot time when practical.

Recommended structure:
- 结构化快照
- 主线判断
- 今日评论与判断
- AI 新闻, including the day's most important 3-5 official/company/model/product updates
- AI 圈博主, only when there is a high-value clue, opinion sample, methodology note, or practice review
- AI 研究前沿, only when there is a high-value paper or research signal
- AI 外围情报观察, only when there is a high-confidence adjacent signal
- GitHub 热门项目
- 值得继续跟踪
- 结构化索引
- 今日结构化结论
- 参考来源

Git requirements:
- Sync with `origin/main` before writing if needed.
- Stage only the generated digest file.
- Commit with `docs: add ai digest for YYYY-MM-DD` or `docs: update ai digest for YYYY-MM-DD` if the file already existed.
- Push to `origin main`.
- Do not use destructive git commands and do not modify unrelated files.
- Report a concise run summary with the report path, covered time window, top themes, key judgments, and pushed commit hash or exact git blocker.
"""
status = "ACTIVE"
rrule = __RRULE_JSON__
model = "gpt-5.5"
reasoning_effort = "high"
execution_environment = "local"
cwds = [__REPO_ROOT_JSON__]
created_at = __CREATED_AT_MS__
